# The camera stays still in the middle of a turn: no refit, no pan to the picked-up piece, no fly-back. After White's first turn the
# camera focuses the board Black must move on (1.25); from there to the Submit the only things that may move it are the player's
# own drag / wheel / keys. `camstill on` fails the script if the zoom or target changes on any frame; `camlog on` prints them.
# Layout (1400x800): Versus (150,250); Standard row (905,224); Play (808,712); Submit (841,90); Undo (558,90).
wait 20
click 150 250        # Versus
wait 30
click 905 224        # Standard
wait 20
click 808 712        # Play
wait 120
clicksq 0 0 e2
wait 30
clicksq 0 0 e4
wait 30
click 841 90         # Submit
wait 90              # the camera hops to Black's board and settles
camexpect state Focus
zoom?
camlog on
camstill on
move 100 400         # hover about
wait 20
clicksq 0 1 e7       # pick up a pawn ...
wait 30
clicksq 0 1 d7       # ... pick up another (switching pieces)
wait 30
clicksq 0 1 d7       # ... put it down again (Clear)
wait 30
clicksq 0 1 e7
wait 30
clicksq 0 1 e5       # a move on the board: the new board appears at the right and the camera does not follow
wait 60
click 558 90         # Undo (the board goes away)
wait 40
clicksq 0 1 e7
wait 30
clicksq 0 1 e5
wait 90
capture camera-still-midturn-after-move
camstill off
camlog off
zoom?
click 841 90         # Submit: now the camera may frame White's board
wait 90
camexpect state Focus
camexpect visible 0 2
capture camera-still-midturn-submitted
